    docs(claude-md): fix LIB MODULES drift vs config/modules.json (#876)

    * docs(claude-md): fix LIB MODULES drift vs config/modules.json

    .claude/CLAUDE.md's "LIB MODULES (18)" list no longer matched the
    governance-protected config/modules.json registry (16 entries):
    content-studio/runtime/session-manager/git-branch-orchestrator/
    external-agent-registry are real lib/ directories missing from the
    registry, and opsly-core is registered but has no lib/opsly-core
    directory (breaks apps/peskids/lib/peskids-shadow-runtime.ts's import).

    Fixes the doc to mirror the registry as it exists today, since
    config/modules.json itself is protected and registering the missing
    modules needs an explicit decision from its owner, not a doc-only PR.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TM2ZqdbVmDRRFRRFzo6mMU

    * docs(claude-md): correct opsly-core claim in the modules drift note

    The previous commit on this PR claimed opsly-core had no real
    directory and that consumers failed to resolve it. Wrong — it's a
    real workspace package at packages/opsly-core (not lib/opsly-core,
    hence it looking "missing" under the LIB MODULES framing), and it
    resolves cleanly once node_modules is actually installed. The earlier
    check ran in a sandbox before npm install had populated node_modules,
    so the resolution failure was a sandbox artifact, not a real bug.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
